{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q19595738","formula":"C₂₀H₂₈FN₃O₃","hill":"C20H28FN3O3","elements":["H","C","N","O","F"],"composition":{"C":20.0,"F":1.0,"H":28.0,"N":3.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"5F-ADB"},"descriptions":{"en":"5F-ADB (also known as MDMB-5F-PINACA using systematic EMCDDA nomenclature and 5F-MDMB-PINACA) is an indazole-based synthetic cannabinoid from the indazole-3-carboxamide family, which has been used as an active ingredient in synthetic cannabis products and has been sold online as a designer drug. 5F-ADB is a potent agonist of the CB1 receptor, though it is unclear whether it is selective for this target. 5F-ADB was first identified in November 2014 from post-mortem samples taken from an individual who had died after using a product containing this substance."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":101895417,"mass":377.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(C)(C)C(C(=O)OC)NC(=O)C1=NN(C2=CC=CC=C21)CCCCCF","inchikey":"PWEKNGSNNAKWBL-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"methyl 2-[[1-(5-fluoropentyl)indazole-3-carbonyl]amino]-3,3-dimethylbutanoate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"101895417","atoms":55,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-3.979,"y":1.141,"z":-2.656,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.563,"y":0.864,"z":-2.113,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.87,"y":-0.111,"z":-3.09,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.774,"y":2.188,"z":-2.108,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.641,"y":0.209,"z":-0.699,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.334,"y":1.102,"z":0.344,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.764,"y":1.937,"z":1.038,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.674,"y":0.849,"z":0.376,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.39,"y":1.629,"z":1.334,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.317,"y":-0.121,"z":-0.178,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.108,"y":-1.19,"z":0.669,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.946,"y":-2.062,"z":0.876,"el":"O"},{"x":0.221,"y":-1.164,"z":1.3,"el":"C"},{"x":1.071,"y":-0.141,"z":1.073,"el":"N"},{"x":2.17,"y":-0.465,"z":1.781,"el":"N"},{"x":2.0